    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A runbook is not a piece of documentation. It is a procedural script someone must execute correctly while tired, under pressure, with paging alerts firing in the background. Every step must be unambiguous to a person who did not write it and may never have run it before.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/runbook-craft/#overview",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "1. The \"fresh machine\" test",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A runbook is only correct if a person who has never run it before, on a freshly provisioned environment, with no tribal context, can complete it successfully.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/runbook-craft/#1-the-fresh-machine-test",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Schedule a quarterly drill where someone who did not author the runbook runs it end-to-end on a sandbox or staging clone. Every pause is a defect in the runbook, not in the runner.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/runbook-craft/#1-the-fresh-machine-test",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Atomic, numbered steps with a verb-first imperative",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Each step performs exactly one action that produces exactly one verifiable result. The verb comes first.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/runbook-craft/#2-atomic-numbered-steps-with-a-verb-first-imperative",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Bad: \"Now we need to make sure that the broker is running and you may also want to check the lag, and if the lag is high then restart things.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/runbook-craft/#2-atomic-numbered-steps-with-a-verb-first-imperative",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Run kafka-broker-api status --broker mdb-prod-1. Expected output: STATUS: HEALTHY.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/runbook-craft/#2-atomic-numbered-steps-with-a-verb-first-imperative",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Run kafka-consumer-groups --describe --group mdb-tam-consumer. Record the LAG column.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/runbook-craft/#2-atomic-numbered-steps-with-a-verb-first-imperative",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "If LAG > 50000, go to step 7 (broker restart). Otherwise continue to step 4.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/runbook-craft/#2-atomic-numbered-steps-with-a-verb-first-imperative",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
