    {
      "title": "Decision Heuristics",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "When to split a runbook: more than 3 levels of branching, more than ~40 atomic steps, or two different audiences.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/runbook-craft/#decision-heuristics",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "When to automate vs. document: a runbook executed > 1x/month and fully deterministic is automation-eligible.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/runbook-craft/#decision-heuristics",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "When to mark a step \"stop and escalate\": any condition the runbook author did not anticipate, any post-condition mismatch.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/runbook-craft/#decision-heuristics",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "When to retire a runbook: the underlying alert hasn't fired in 12 months and the system has changed.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/runbook-craft/#decision-heuristics",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
